  "limitations": [
    "Diagnostic evidence only. The full first declaration did not complete; no qualification or global counter increment is supported.",
    "The collector begins before human.admit. Its clock origin differs from Portfolio21/attempt-18; counts and times do not establish a causal before/after performance comparison.",
    "All bucket values are cumulative at an observed checkpoint. Inclusive times overlap, are rounded to integer milliseconds, and must not be summed into total CPU or wall time.",
    "canonical.digest measures digestSfValue only. It excludes direct canonicalSfValue calls, including plannerRequestIdentity, and does not measure all canonicalization or all CPU work.",
    "root.caller.* instruments PlannerCalculationServices only. It does not cover the direct Finance caller. Missing root.caller buckets do not mean Root was unused, and this profile alone does not attribute each Root invocation to Finance.",
    "state.read.identity-absent aggregates read namespaces and arbitrary callbacks. It is not a count of missed selectSfCaseIdentity opportunities.",
    "The baseline-accessor branch rejects an unsupported accessor before comparing its getter/setter identities. That reason would not prove getter/setter equality. No such rejection bucket was observed here.",
    "root.physical.callback counts callback entries, not independently identified physical roots, committed transactions, accepted roots, or completed requests.",
    "The two clone spans include the original callback and await, not just clone work. Their populations differ, so their average durations are not a controlled speed comparison.",
    "Zero drops/errors/skips is reported at the five emitted checkpoints. There is no final snapshot; the last HTTP span remains pending. The archive does not prove a complete backend unwind or completion after 50 seconds.",
    "Absent buckets are observations within this one diagnostic frame and emitted prefix only. Counts do not establish per-object joins or behavior outside the frame.",
    "The collector adds bookkeeping and output overhead without replacing intrinsics, wrapping providers, or making additional authority/provider calls."
  ]
}
